  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV AIDS Prevention and Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD (Catholic Agency for Overseas Development) has been working in partnership with Church in Zambia to support various development and relief programmes. Since April 2005, CAFOD has been supporting the Sisters of the Sacred Heart of Jesus and Mary to implement the Households in Distress (HID) Project in Mbala Deanery. The Mbala HID project was designed to slow down the spread of HIV and contribute to the reduction of the impact of the HIV and AIDS on families in Mbala and Mpulungu districts. The three-year funding cycle for Mbala HID has came to an end. CAFOD and the partner made an assessment of the project and what came out strongly is the need to integrate HIV and AIDS with livelihoods activities. 

The programme is building on the lessons learnt from the implementation of the Village orphan support  livelihoods and psychosocial support programme. The Mbala evaluation of 2009 and the new programme developed then led to the need to scale up an integrrated HIV and livelihoods programme for Mbala.The project will draw on its experience and linkages with other programmes in Zambia supported by CAFOD and in the region and  increase  the understanding of the Livelihoods integrated HIV &amp; AIDS response,  causes of poverty and injustice. CAFOD will support partners and communities to implement an integrated livelihoods and HIV&amp;AIDS programme while challenging their government at provincial and national level to adopt and implement HIV &amp; AIDS, Livelihoods and other policies that promote social justice and end poverty.

The  programme for Mbala will: 
1. Make follow ups on recommendations made through consultative meeting with partners and stakeholders in Mbala and the National Office on the nature of the programme.
2. Review and lessons learning from existing programmes and projects and take up some of the recommendations from the current partner&#x2019;s evaluation conducted and scale- up the programme. through:
&#x2022; Capacity strengthening of partners and communities in various issues
&#x2022; HIV and AIDS (prevention, mitigation, treatment, care and support)
&#x2022; Advocacy
&#x2022; Gender&#x2013;based violence, to be addressed as it cannot be ignored within the context of Mbala - in Zambia, both from an HIV and AIDS perspective and gender equality as an issue of social justice.
&#x2022; Food security &#x2013; livelihoods within the context of HIV and AIDS.</narrative>
  </description>
